.terraform
.idea
.DS_Store
.env*
!.env.aws.template
!.env.gcp.template
!/.envrc
.last_used_env
.tfplan.*
*.tfvars

# --- SIG: deployment config is TRACKED, credentials are NOT -------------------
# Upstream ignores every .env and .tfvars because upstream's may carry secrets.
# Ours do not: they hold CIDRs, bucket names, AMI ids, instance types, cluster
# sizes and a public ACM ARN — nothing credential-bearing. Ignoring them made
# the entire CommonQuant deployment config exist on exactly one laptop, with no
# history, no review and no recovery path. That is a worse failure than the one
# the blanket ignore was guarding against.
#
# The invariant, enforced by scripts/config-preflight.sh (run it in CI and
# before apply): credentials live in AWS Secrets Manager and are referenced by
# id from these files, never inlined. The preflight fails closed if a
# secret-shaped value appears in anything tracked here.
#
# Named per account so which cloud a file describes is never ambiguous.
!.env.dev
!iac/provider-aws/dev.cq.tfvars
!iac/provider-aws/dev.sig.tfvars.reference
terraform.tfstate
terraform.tfstate.backup
**/.tfplan.*
tests/periodic-test/build-template/e2b.toml
.air
go.work.sum
.infisical.json
.vscode/mise-tools
/packages/fc-kernels
/packages/fc-versions

# Local downloads & build artifacts
.kernels/
.fc-versions/
*.zip
errored.tfstate
*.tfstate.backup
domain.tf.cloudflare-upstream
wake-response.json

# pnpm lock files (generated)
pnpm-lock.yaml

# COST-00 P3: per-account Terraform working dirs and local plan artifacts
iac/provider-aws/.terraform-*/
*.tfplan
*.sig-backup
**/bin/

# Local proof receipts are regenerated per exact commit
.sig/proofs/
